@bio:

Frans Wiering is a (retired) Associate Professor at the
Music Information Computing group of the Department of
Information and Computing Sciences of Utrecht University
(Netherlands). His PhD thesis ‘The Language of the Modes'
(1995) investigates the richness and variety of modality in
16th- and 17th-century polyphony. His research is in
computational musicology, music information retrieval and
interactive technologies. Recently he published about the
acceptance of new technologies in music research (‘What
Do Musicologists Do All Day’, with Charles Inskip),
user-centred design in corpus creation (CORSICA), and big
data analysis of tonal structures in early music
(CANTOSTREAM, with Mirjam Visscher).


@@END: BIO